From: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: bcm - use the fallback for an ICV size SPU-M cannot handle

SPU-M takes the ICV size in 32-bit words, so the driver truncates a
digest size that is not a multiple of 4. The SPU then inserts or
checks a shorter ICV than requested:

  alg: aead: gcm-aes-iproc encryption test failed (wrong result) on
  test vector "random: alen=131 plen=3965 authsize=15 klen=32
  novrfy=0", ...

Use the fallback for these digest sizes on SPU-M. All the AEADs have
one.

Fixes: 9d12ba86f818 ("crypto: brcm - Add Broadcom SPU driver")
Signed-off-by: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
@@ -2608,6 +2608,12 @@ static int aead_need_fallback(struct aead_request *req)
 		return 1;
 	}
 
+	if ((spu->spu_type == SPU_TYPE_SPUM) && (ctx->digestsize % 4)) {
+		flow_log("%s() SPU-M needs fallback for digest size %d\n",
+			 __func__, ctx->digestsize);
+		return 1;
+	}
+
 	/*
 	 * SPU-M on NSP has an issue where AES-CCM hash is not correct
 	 * when AAD size is 0
